{{also|Parry}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|parree}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|en|parree}}, from {{inh|en|enm|*parree}}, {{m|enm|*paree}}, from {{der|en|fro|paree||preparation, ceremony, parade}}, from {{der|en|ML.|parāta||preparation, parade}}, from {{m|la|parāre||to ward off, guard, defend, prepare, get ready}}. More at {{m|en|pare}}. The English verb is taken from the noun. {{doublet|en|parade}}.

Alternative etymology derives the verb ''parry'' from {{der|en|fr|parez}}, the imperative form of {{m|fr|parer||to fend off}}, ultimately from the {{der|en|ML.|parāre}}. See above.

